{"parentUuid":"c138012e-357e-4bb8-a21b-9c8e1c199ad2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8vH5Zdo4z6xtCPUWeqM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014ZqcP6Ts2GEUdA5m92eE2z","name":"mcp__github__create_pull_request","input":{"owner":"missingbulb","repo":"Shepherd","title":"Carry the fleet usage aggregate over from Sheepdog","head":"claude/carry-fleet-usage-history","base":"main","body":"`usage-fleet.GENERATED.json`, copied verbatim from `missingbulb/Sheepdog@main` — 12 day rows, 5 week rows, 12 folding members, 460 KB.\n\nThis was deliberately left out of #23 on the reasoning that Shepherd's own `fleet-usage` task recomputes the file daily, so nothing is lost. That was only half right. The recompute *is* stateless, but its inputs are each member's own `.claudinite/local/usage.GENERATED.json` over the window that member still keeps — so a fresh run would start the series from a shorter history than the one Sheepdog had accumulated, and the earlier weeks would simply not come back.\n\nIt is a `GENERATED` file, so it is copied rather than edited, and the next `fleet-usage` run rewrites it in place.\n\n`.gitattributes` gains the `merge=ours` entry the `generated-merge-driver` check asked for once the file landed — without it a conflicting merge on a generated file gets hand-resolved and desyncs from its source. World sweep is clean with it.\n\nFixes #30\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":666,"cache_read_input_tokens":379128,"output_tokens":587,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":666,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2