{"parentUuid":"84bc1d58-063f-4d28-9310-16efcffad755","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"Move fleet-digest task into packs/sheepdog/tasks/fleet-digest/","description":"Copy task.md, task.mjs, worker.mjs, collect-fleet-day.mjs, digest-config.mjs from Sheepdog's local pack; rewrite the mount-relative imports to canon-relative ones; generalize the \"why it's local\" prose.","activeForm":"Moving the fleet-digest task into canon","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Land digest-plain-text and dated-fixture-collision as sheepdog checks","description":"Move both checks into the pack, wire them into pack.mjs worldRules, fix their doc: paths and mount-scope skips for canon.","activeForm":"Landing the two digest checks","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Port the tests into packs-tests/sheepdog/tasks/fleet-digest/","description":"collect-fleet-day, worker, digest-config, digest-plain-text, dated-fixture-collision test files, rewritten to canon's packs-tests import style. See them fail first where possible.","activeForm":"Porting the digest tests","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Update sheepdog pack docs, version and config schema","description":"pack.mjs header + version bump, RULES.md, README.md, the digest config block on the config schema, and the digests/README.md series doc. Run the full canon check/test suite.","activeForm":"Updating pack docs and version","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":4},"type":"attachment","uuid":"205ca4e1-f386-420f-bff2-f457f4bfef60","timestamp":"2026-08-17T20:03:54.828Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote","cwd":"/home/user/Shepherd","sessionId":"be45aff4-0993-5089-8959-570a08bb6d85","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"claude/carry-fleet-usage-history"}
{"parentUuid":"205ca4e1-f386-420f-bff2-f457f4bfef60","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8vHkFZJV2TGcpoZbc6x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Comment class: other\n\n**Both merged.** [Claudinite#958](https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/pull/958) → `ca20111` (closes [#954](https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/954)); [Shepherd#29](https://github.com/missingbulb/Shepherd/pull/29) → `9f20e04` (closes [#28](https://github.com/missingbulb/Shepherd/issues/28)). `fleet-digest` is canon now, and Shepherd will pick it up on its next nightly converge. Local `main` synced, conversation captured (639 entries).\n\n**Usage file carried over** — [PR #31](https://github.com/missingbulb/Shepherd/pull/31), [issue #30](https://github.com/missingbulb/Shepherd/issues/30). Copied verbatim from `Sheepdog@main`: 12 day rows, 5 week rows, 12 folding members.\n\nYou were right to reverse that call, and my earlier reasoning for skipping it was wrong in a way worth naming: I said the daily recompute makes the file lossless. The recompute is stateless, but its *inputs* are each member's own aggregate over the window that member still keeps — so a fresh run would have started the series short, and the earlier weeks would not have come back.\n\nLanding it also surfaced a check I'd have otherwise missed: `generated-merge-driver` fired advisory on the new file, so `.gitattributes` gains `usage-fleet.GENERATED.json merge=ours`. World sweep clean.\n\nOne correction to my previous answer: I said Shepherd doesn't declare `grow_with_claudinite`. It does — the declaration is there. What's true is that it hasn't *run* `usage-fold` yet, so it has no `.claudinite/local/usage.GENERATED.json` and will show in the fleet file's `coverage.absent` as \"not folding yet\" until its first fold. The conclusion was right, the reason I gave was not.\n\n> ⚠️ Still open: [Shepherd#31](https://github.com/missingbulb/Shepherd/pull/31) awaiting your call (CI running). Now that #958 has landed, `missingbulb/Sheepdog` is free to retire — its scheduler is already stood down ([Sheepdog#249](https://github.com/missingbulb/Sheepdog/pull/249)). Shepherd's [`digests/README.md`](https://github.com/missingbulb/Shepherd/blob/main/digests/README.md) still says the task lives \"in this repo's own local pack\", now stale. Still undecided: whether the enforcer's ~360-line `RULES.md` of lessons gets extracted before Sheepdog goes."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":904,"cache_read_input_tokens":379794,"output_tokens":901,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":904,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":901,"cache_read_input_tokens":379794,"cache_creation_input_tokens":904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":904},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8vHha5Xmfne8uGWV24z","attributionMcpServer":"github","attributionMcpTool":"create_pull_request","type":"assistant","uuid":"50b70d56-81f2-462f-8e2a-5fa7fcb4db55","timestamp":"2026-08-17T20:04:07.331Z","effort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote","cwd":"/home/user/Shepherd","sessionId":"be45aff4-0993-5089-8959-570a08bb6d85","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"claude/carry-fleet-usage-history"}
